module gunbc.auth.deployment_gate_authorization

// WHICH AUTHORIZATION PERFORMS THE PRIVILEGED EFFECT "answer a pending environment gate for a run",
// and everything that decision needs: which credential kind may make the review call, what the broker
// must confirm before it posts, and what must be witnessed before a human reviewer is removed.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN THOSE ANSWERS SITTING IN extdeps.github.
// DESIGN.md §3 splits interface, realization and policy three ways, and §3b's External facts boundary
// puts product policy and this repository's own observations in the consuming layer. The upstream model
// says what GitHub ACCEPTS; a decision made here can change without editing a dependency model, and a
// reader of the upstream file is not told what our broker does. Concretely: GitHub accepts an operator
// OAuth/PAT call at this endpoint, and REFUSING it is our policy, not GitHub's — so the refusal is
// here and the accepted set is there.
//
// AND WHY NOTHING IN IT IS A TEST OR A FIXTURE. On main no dag/gunbc/auth module carries a `test fn`;
// the tests for this file live in test.claim.deployment_gate_authorization_witness, which is
// where fixtures belong. A production module that ships fixtures ships values someone can mistake for
// observations, and a typed prerequisite built from a fixture is the prose guard it replaced wearing a
// type. What is kept here are types, folds, and the one frontier row that says "not yet".
//
// WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT DO. It grants nothing, touches no GitHub setting, and cannot be executed
// against GitHub. It is the model stage-2 code is written against.

